Sample Input and Output:

Enter the size of the array
3
Enter the 3 array elements
1 2 3
Expected Output:
1 3 6 2 5 3
3
6
2
5
3

1. Brute Force
Code: T.C: O(N^3),    O(1)- Auxially space, O(N) - Total space bcoz i made an array to input elements of an array.


   static void PrintAllSubArrays(int[] arr){
	    int n = arr.length;
		for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
          for(int j=i;j<n;j++){
            int sum = 0;
			for(int k=i;k<=j;k++){
				sum = sum + arr[k];
			}
			System.out.print(sum+" ");
		  }
	   }
   }
2. Better 
Code: T.C: O(N^2),    S.C: O(N) - Auxillary space


   static void PrintAllSubArrays(int[] arr){
	    int n = arr.length;
        int[] prefix = new int[n];               //1. Creating an array to store prefix sum
        prefix[0] = arr[0];
        for(int i=1;i<n;i++){                     
            prefix[i] = prefix[i-1] + arr[i];    //2. Calculating prefix sum and storing at indexes.
        }
        
		for(int i=0;i<n;i++){                    //3. Start point is fixed and increments once j runs from i till end
          for(int j=i;j<n;j++){                  //4. j runs from i till end
             int sum = (i==0)? prefix[j]:prefix[j] - prefix[i-1]; 
// if start point is index 0 then just retrieve prefix sum of those indexes . 
//but if start index is 1 or 2 and so on then you have calculate prefix sum :
//from that starting point till j by considering prefix sum of j and subtracting the prefix sum of just before the starting point(i-1)
             System.out.print(sum+" ");
             }
	    }
	} 
   

